# Protected Paths (AD-16). This file is itself Protected, by `/conformance/`.
#
# One CODEOWNERS-style pattern per line; `#` comments and blank lines are
# ignored. A `!` prefix marks an exclusion: the last active entry that matches a
# path decides it. A trailing ` after-phase:<n>` marks an entry that is active
# only once `decisions/PHASE-<n>-EXIT.md` exists. The check matches inclusions
# in any letter case and exclusions case-sensitively; CODEOWNERS keeps the
# literal pattern, so a PR touching a case variant (e.g. `claude.md`) gets no
# automatic Code Owner request; request @edanisko's review by hand.
#
# `.github/CODEOWNERS` is generated from this list:
#   bun run protected-paths:codeowners

